  "framing": "A wide cinematic cutaway seen straight on from the side, like a doll's house with its front wall removed, filling the whole frame. A standing adult would be about a fifth of the image height and a doorway a little taller. Lit at night by its own lamps. No text, no captions, no border.",
  "prompt": "A cross-section of an old two-storey concrete shop building on a city street at night. The ground floor, from about the middle of the image down to a thick concrete floor slab a little above the bottom, and across the middle two thirds of the width, is the fixer's small radio repair shop, lit warm and dim by a desk lamp and two bare fluorescent tubes. Above it, the upper floor is a dim, bare room with one bare bulb. Below the shop's floor, the slab and a dark cellar. On the left, outside the building, the wet street at night in thick amber-brown smog with a street lamp and smokestacks; on the right, the next building's dark wall in the smog. The shop, from left to right: in its left wall, the shop's street door; a tall bookshelf of swollen books and gutted radios; a battered leather sofa with a checked blanket and a floor lamp beside it; a wooden back door standing ajar on a dark back room; a long wooden workbench at hip height with drawers, on it an old monitor with a green line on its screen, an oscilloscope, an opened radio and a desk lamp on an arm; above the bench, within reach, a pegboard of ordinary hand tools and above that a shelf of patched radios and a wall clock; a corkboard with a map and pinned notes; a low cabinet with a ripped-open old visor on a stand; in the right wall, a bolted side door. Every radio and device is an old relic patched together over decades: dull grey metal, valves, dials and cables. The shop's floor is worn floorboards, flat and clear to walk along from end to end. No people.",
  "concierge": "A cross-section of an old two-storey shop building on a city street at night, as the city AI shows it, like a doll's house with its front wall removed. The ground floor, from about the middle of the image down to a thick floor slab a little above the bottom, and across the middle two thirds of the width, is a lovingly kept antique radio shop, warm, cosy and glamorous in a nostalgic way, lit by warm amber lamps. Upstairs, a warm red-orange bar with glowing globe lamps, lush plants and a pink neon ring. Below the shop's floor, the slab and a dark cellar. On the left, outside the building, a glossy wet street mirroring violet, blue, pink and cyan neon, a sleek street lamp and a glittering city of neon towers behind; on the right, the next building's wall touched by neon. The shop, from left to right: in its left wall, a polished wooden street door; a tall bookshelf of books and restored radios; a supple leather sofa with a soft wool blanket and a floor lamp beside it; a polished wooden back door standing ajar on a warm back room; a long polished wooden workbench at hip height with drawers, on it a handsome vintage monitor with a soft green screen, an oscilloscope, an opened radio and a brass desk lamp on an arm; above the bench, within reach, a tidy pegboard of polished tools and above that a shelf of restored radios in walnut, cream bakelite and brass with warm glowing dials, and a wall clock; a framed map of the city; a low cabinet with a white visor on a stand, glowing soft blue; in the right wall, a door marked STAFF in brass letters. The shop's floor is polished floorboards, flat and clear to walk along from end to end. No people.",
